nd on the brink of death  toga  suddenly experiences a quirk awakening  and she becomes capable of not only  transforming into someone else  physically but she also learns to  actually use that person's quirk in that  moment she is able to transform into or  Chico and use or Chacos quirk zero  gravity what's more she is able to use a  quirk very effectively against a large  number of enemies at the same time it  seems that after the  illusion of her quark toga is now able  to copy and use the quirk of anyone that  she transforms into as long as she has  seen the quark in action and knows how  it works  needless to say while the ability to  change her physical appearance into  someone else was useful for spying and  Intel gathering the power to also copy  that persitz quark changes the game  completely  as long as toga consumes enough blood  from multiple people she is able to  transform into those different people at  will and with her awakened quark this  means that she will now be able to use  all of their quirks in battle I'm sure  this will take some training to master  but by learning the ability to copy  quirks on top of just copying someone's  physical appearance toga has transformed  into a completely new villain a villain  that is far more dangerous than she was  before now let's talk about another  member of the league of villains the one  and only twice get it I said one and  only but his whole thing is making  clones of himself  anyway twice is the mentally disturbed  villain who is capable of creating  clones of himself or others as long as  he knows the precise measurements and  characteristics of that which he is  copying the clones that twice creates  will not be as strong as the original  and if the clones take enough damage  they will simply dissolve into mud the  amount of damage required to destroy a  clone is roughly equivalent to suffering  a broken limb when we first meet him  twice doesn't want to make clone 2  himself because in the past his clones  began fighting over who is the real  twice and who is the clone and this led  to complete chaos so instead of cloning  himself twice uses his quirk to create  clones of other members of the league of  villains such as Dobby but he can only  create two clones at a time however  eventually twice becomes willing to make  clones of himself again and in Chapter  230 his quirk evolves in such a way that  he is able to create a virtually  infinite amount of clones his clones  start making more clones and they  multiply rapidly filling up entire city  blocks and absolutely overwhelming every  opponent in sight with the sheer  strength of numbers it has been  suggested that if his quark is used to  its full potential  twice could over  an entire country by himself now my  inclusion of twice here might be a bit  controversial because his ability to  create infinite doubles could just be  classified as a super move called sad  man's parade so it's not necessarily  that his quirk has fundamentally changed  rather he was able to finally overcome  the trauma of cloning himself in the  past which allowed him to clone himself  again and then those clones clone  themselves in turn since they all  possess the same quirk and then before  you know it an army of twice's  appears nevertheless due to the drastic  difference that twice's use of the  infinite doubles makes in battle  compared to any other use of his quirk I  have to count double as one of the  strongest quirks that has changed since  the story began his quirk may not have  changed on a biological level but going  from making only one or two clones of  other people to an army of clones that  can overwhelm entire cities and perhaps  even countries is a drastic change in  the use of his quirk that I simply  cannot ignore any pro hero including the  very strongest ones would have a very  difficult time dealing with twice as  powers as they are right now and that is  why he simply has to be on this list now  let's talk 