ven different quirks that  will one day all be at the disposal of  its user the quark I'm talking about is  none other than one for all and the user  is of course Deku after a strange black  substance begins emanating from Deku in  Chapter 210 it is eventually revealed  that Deku is going to manifest six more  quirks on top of the quark that he  already possesses which is one for all  this is because the quark one for all  itself is growing and as a quirk that  stockpiles power and then transfers  those powers on to other users one for  all has actually been stockpiling the  different quark factors of its previous  holders within its core with that said  no previous user of one for all was ever  able to use the other six quirks but for  some reason dec who has started  manifesting these additional quirks so  far he has only been able to manifest  one of the six additional quirks and  that quirk is called black whip as the  name suggests this quirk allows its user  to generate powerful black whips from  his body and these whips can be used to  grab  and people dec who is unable to use the  whips effectively at first and he needed  to practice and train before he could  make effective use of this new quirk  when I first read the manga and saw this  development when I realized that deca  was going to be manifesting six more  quirks on top of the already overpowered  quirk that he possesses I was pretty  disappointed  Deku is already so insanely op4 a mere  high school student and when we take  into account that he inherited his quirk  later on in life it didn't have his  entire life to learn how to use it even  his current powers and abilities are  arguably quite broken so when I learned  that on top of that deck who would be  able to use six more powerful quirks I  had no idea what horikoshi was thinking  and I'm still pretty iffy about this  revelation because I do think that Deku  is more than strong enough as he is now  but the arc that followed this  revelation in